  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: S2h external skill hardening: structured risk report at inspection (scripts, endpoints, tools, credential references, dependencies, filesystem) gating quarantined to testing (P21)",
  "spec": "orchestrator/skill_discovery.inspect(): extend the report with risk = {scripts: [{path, shebang or extension, executable bit}], endpoints: [hosts and URLs found in any file], tools: [names from the skill frontmatter allowed-tools or tools fields and Bash/shell mentions], credential_refs: [environment variable names matching KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD|PASSWD|CREDENTIAL|AUTH and mentions of dotenv or credential files, names only], dependencies: [packages from requirements, pyproject, package.json, pip or npm install lines], filesystem: [absolute paths, home-directory references, recursive delete or chmod commands], scan: the context_scanner verdict per file from S1d, level: low|medium|high with reasons}. Level rules: high when scan is blocked anywhere, or an endpoint plus a credential_ref both appear, or a recursive delete or permission change appears, or a dependency is installed from a URL or git source; medium when any script, endpoint, dependency or credential_ref exists; low otherwise. The report is persisted in the existing findings.json (no new file). orchestrator/skills_registry.transition(): a quarantined skill may move to testing only when its latest inspection report exists, its content hash matches, and level is not high and scan is not blocked; otherwise raise ValueError naming the reasons unless the transition reason starts with 'human-reviewed:' (record that in the state document). CLI: `orchestrator skills inspect <id>` prints the risk report; `skills list` shows the level. Docs: docs/hermes-hardening/14-skill-hardening.md.\nSpec review T-1122 folded in: (1) No new file: the risk report is a new top-level key risk inside the existing findings.json (the file the tests already assert), so the content-hash listings in inspect(), check_upstream() and skills_registry._testing_findings() need no change; drop every mention of inspection.json. (2) The level gate WRAPS the existing _testing_findings() control rather than replacing it: the old blocks (block-severity finding, presence of a script) stay exactly as today, the new rule adds a block when level is high or scan_overall is blocked, and the existing 'override:' reason prefix keeps working alongside 'human-reviewed:' (both bypass, both recorded in the state document with the reason). (3) rollback() re-enters testing through the same wrapped gate, so both paths apply one bar; existing tests at tests/test_skill_discovery.py that assert findings.json content equality keep passing (extend their expected dicts with the risk key where they compare whole reports).\nSpec review T-1129 folded in: (a) the base text now says findings.json only. (b) rollback(): the bypass check looks at the ORIGINAL transition reason recorded in the state document for the last quarantined-to-testing move (the 'rollback: ' prefix that rollback() prepends never hides it), so a skill approved with override: or human-reviewed: rolls back into testing without re-approval, while one never approved is blocked; test both. (c) `skills list` prints '-' in the level column for any skill without a quarantine findings.json (builtin, active, never inspected). (d) risk.scan is the same dict object inspect() already computed for the top-level scan key (copied by reference, never recomputed).\nRepository rules: unittest (not pytest), tests/_harness.py single ORCH_ROOT fixture; every acceptance test id tests/test_<module>.py::test_name is a method def test_name(self) in a unittest.TestCase. No new third-party dependencies. Never write secret values to any file or log; test fixtures use synthetic names and values that are not credential-shaped. Do not quote template placeholder tokens (double braces) anywhere in code comments or docs. Shadow-first: a new adaptive path never changes what a worker sees until its mode is active; shadow only writes decision_log or runs rows. Run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until green; the base suite must stay green. Do not ask questions: decide, and note decisions in the result summary. The interface contracts of the stage 1 modules are in .orchestrator/plan.md (section GOAL T-0991) and in docs/hermes-hardening/0*.md on this branch; read the merged module before building on it.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1132"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_skill_discovery.py::test_risk_report_levels_from_fixture_skills (a benign skill low, a script-plus-endpoint skill medium, an endpoint-plus-credential skill high, a blocked-scan skill high)",
    "tests/test_skills_registry.py::test_quarantined_to_testing_blocked_on_high_risk_unless_human_reviewed",
    "tests/test_skills_registry.py::test_transition_requires_matching_inspection_hash",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_skills_inspect_prints_risk_level",
    "tests/test_skills_registry.py::test_rollback_uses_the_same_wrapped_gate (a high-risk skill cannot re-enter testing via rollback without an override or human-reviewed reason; a script-only skill is still blocked as before)",
    "tests/test_skills_registry.py::test_rollback_keeps_original_override_reason (an override-approved skill rolls back into testing; a never-approved high-risk skill is blocked)",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_skills_list_level_dash_without_report",
